Critical bug: If the delete operation fails, the function still returns `missingSchemaIds` and sync continues. This will cause upsert_concepts to refuse schemas with names that match the stale schemas that failed to delete - the exact issue this PR aims to fix.

The delete error is only logged, not propagated. If deletion fails, the sync should either:
1. Throw an error to stop the sync
2. Return an empty Set to prevent attempting to sync schemas that will be refused

Current behavior:
```typescript
if (deleteError)
  console.error("Could not delete stale schemas:", deleteError);
// continues and returns missingSchemaIds anyway
return missingSchemaIds;
```

Should be:
```typescript
if (deleteError) {
  console.error("Could not delete stale schemas:", deleteError);
  return new Set(); // Don't try to sync if we couldn't delete stale schemas
}
```
```suggestion

    const { error: deleteError } = await supabaseClient
      .from("Concept")
      .delete()
      .eq("space_id", spaceId)
      .eq("is_schema", true)
      .in("source_local_id", [...staleSchemaIds]);
    if (deleteError) {
      console.error("Could not delete stale schemas:", deleteError);
      return new Set(); // Don't try to sync if we couldn't delete stale schemas
    }
  }
  return missingSchemaIds;

```


